  "query_preview": "..A strong trough over the Pacific Northwest states \nwill continue to dig southward. This will result in continued dry \nconditions and gusty southwest winds across the region. The pressure \ngradient will remain very tight through Sunday, with very strong \nsouthwest winds 15-30 mph with gusts to 45-55 mph today through \nSunday. Winds will drop off a bit as we head into tonight will \nremain elevated into Sunday. Winds will gradually diminish Sunday \nnight. Wind Advisories are in effect through Sunday evening for much \nof northern Arizona. Winds then diminish for Monday and into next \nweek but stay gusty, remaining below advisory criteria.  \n\nWith the strong winds and very dry conditions in place, we will \ncontinue to see critical fire weather conditioning through Sunday.\nA Red Flag Warning is in effect for all of northern Arizona through \nSunday. While it won't be nearly as windy as we head into the new \nweek, near-critical fire weather conditions are expected to \ncontinue. Areas across eastern Arizona (mainly in the Little \nColorado River Valley) look to be the most likely location for any \nadditional Red Flag Warnings on Monday though we will hold off on \nissuing any additional headlines for now. \n\nThe trough remains across the western United States through much of \nthe week. Some moisture may try to push in from the east towards the \nholiday weekend but confidence is low at this time.",
